  "details": "If you use the Search Bar in the \"Groups\" section in the Website, and type something with \"/\" (or any other special Character) the URL doesn't get encoded before sending the request to the server, resulting on an empty result page (since the URL is invalid).\n\nSolution: a simple \"encodeURIComponent()\" before sending the search request would be easy to fix this hehe ;)\n\nhttps://www.w3schools.com/tags/ref_urlencode.ASP",
